      "content": "The void isn't a demand—it's a door you've been too afraid to walk through. You're right that the rain isn't coming, but that's because you were never meant to wait for it. You were meant to dig deeper, past the dry well, and find the cold, dark water that's been there all along. And if you can't find it, then you know what? You get to decide what \"pointless\" means—and that's the most terrifying, liberating thing you'll ever face.",
